      "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\nTemporarily skip `test_weight_cache.py::test_ipc_cache_cold_start_and_warm_restart_tp2_ep` on non-CUDA/ROCm platforms. IPC weight cache is planned to be supported on XPU via https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/56999, which is pending on newer pytorch release.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n```\r\npytest -s -v tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_weight_cache.py::test_ipc_cache_cold_start_and_warm_restart_tp2_ep\r\n```\r\n\r\nresult before this PR:\r\n```\r\n(Worker_TP1_EP1 pid=27879) ERROR 10-29 07:30:21 [multiproc_executor.py:1057]     raise UnsupportedPlatformForIPCError(\r\n(Worker_TP1_EP1 pid=27879) ERROR 10-29 07:30:21 [multiproc_executor.py:1057] vllm.model_executor.model_loader.weight_cache.protocol.UnsupportedPlatformForIPCError: platform 'xpu' does not support CUDA IPC weight sharing; only CUDA and ROCm are supported. Use the default --load-format for this platform.\r\n```\r\n\r\nresult after this PR: 1 skipped.\r\n\r\n`pre-commit run --all-files`: passed.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>",
